SURGEON: Dr. K. Ophthalmology
PROCEDURE: Left eye phacoemulsification with IOL implantation
SCHEDULED: 07/22/2024

HPI: Patient presents for routine pre-operative evaluation for elective cataract surgery. Cataract diagnosed 18 months ago, progressive visual decline (20/80 OS). No diabetes, no steroid use, no prior ocular surgery. Reports mild dry eye, managed with OTC artificial tears PRN. No flashes, floaters, curtain vision loss.

PMH: Hypertension (controlled, lisinopril 10mg daily), Osteoarthritis (acetaminophen PRN), Hypothyroidism (levothyroxine 75mcg daily). No CAD, CHF, Afib, COPD, CKD. No bleeding diathesis.

MEDS: Lisinopril 10mg PO daily, Levothyroxine 75mcg PO daily, Acetaminophen 500mg PRN, Artificial tears PRN OS. No anticoagulants, antiplatelets, steroids.

ALLERGIES: NKDA

SOCIAL: Non-smoker, rare ETOH, lives with spouse, independent ADLs.

