Ocular: VA 20/30 OD, 20/80 OS. IOP 16 OD, 17 OS. Slit lamp: 2+ nuclear sclerotic cataract OS, clear cornea, quiet AC. Fundus: CDR 0.4 OU, no DR.

LABS: CBC, BMP, PT/INR, PTT all WNL (drawn 07/08/2024). ECG: NSR, no acute changes.

ASSESSMENT: Low surgical risk (ASA Class II). No contraindications to elective cataract surgery under topical/local anesthesia. Continue all current medications perioperatively. No bridging needed.

PLAN: Cleared for surgery 07/22/2024. Hold morning lisinopril day of surgery per anesthesia protocol. Resume post-op. Standard post-op regimen: Prednisolone acetate 1% QID x 1 wk, taper; Moxifloxacin QID x 1 wk; Ketorolac QID x 2 wk. Follow-up 1-day, 1-wk, 1-mo post-op.

